# `QuantumSystem` — a sub-composite holding a single quantum-state map
# on its bridge. Designed for use as a typed `map[QuantumSystem]` entry
# (per quantum-lifecycle.ys and quantum-cross-cnot.ys).
#
# Key piece: the internal `Publish` process re-emits `state` every tick
# so the bridge tap carries the snapshot up to the parent. Without it
# the bridge would only emit deltas of inner state changes; an initial
# state would never become visible to a parent step. (See
# `docs/merge-protocol.md` for the "snapshot-publish on bridge" pattern
# — symmetric apply at the input bridge + a publish process at the
# output is what lets a parent observe a sub-composite's current
# state through the bridge without piercing the composite boundary.)
#
# State shape: `map[float]` keyed by bitstring (`'0'`, `'1'` for a
# single qubit; `'00'/'01'/'10'/'11'` for a 2-qubit joint state).
# Size is implicit in the keyset — the lifecycle (split/merge)
# mutates it freely as factorize/tensor change the structure.

# Republish state each tick as an `overwrite[map[float]]` update so the
# bridge carries the current snapshot. The Overwrite wrap forces a
# replace (not additive merge) at the inner slot.
process Publish ~{state :: map[float]} ->{state :: overwrite[map[float]]}
(
  {state: state}
)

composite QuantumSystem[state0 :: map[float] = {'0': 1.0, '1': 0.0}]
  ~{state :: map[float] @ state = state0}
  ->{state :: overwrite[map[float]] @ state}
(
  state: state0 |
  publish: Publish ~{state: state} ->{state: state}
)
